WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.480
Two soldiers dead near Hebron. Israel orders a West Bank wide closure before Tuesday's election.

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:12.040
This is Omni View Top World News, episode 31. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host.

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:16.600
After that closure, a White House claim of a local pause in occupied Ukraine,

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:21.260
then a church funeral attacked in Jordan, then a terrorism inquiry outside Paris.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:26.760
The Israel Defense Forces say two Palestinian gunmen opened fire Friday at a temporary checkpoint

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:30.120
outside Hebron after they failed to reach a nearby highway.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:33.100
The military believes they meant to attack civilians there.

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:38.560
The Globe and Mail names the dead soldiers as Staff Sergeant Ron Yonatan Roitman, 23,

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:41.360
and Sergeant Yuval Shai's film, 20.

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:44.540
That account says three other Israelis were lightly wounded.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:49.940
The Guardian says a preliminary military investigation found the gunfight lasted more than 20 minutes

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:53.280
and left five Israelis wounded, two of whom later died.

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:58.800
The Army says both Palestinians, from Hebron, were armed with an M-16 and a handgun,

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:00.880
and were killed near the Yehuda Junction.

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:07.380
An AFP photographer who saw the battle reported two men with a handgun and an automatic rifle exchanging fire.

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:12.180
Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's office says it ordered Hebron cordoned off at once

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:14.700
and a full closure of the West Bank from Friday.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:18.520
The Guardian calls it the fourth territory-wide restriction in a month.

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:21.920
Gates that linked Palestinian villages to major roads shut

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:25.180
while Israeli drivers, including settlers, can still pass.

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:29.280
Netanyahu says forces will evacuate residents of the attacker's neighborhood.

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:33.940
Go house to house, seize weapons, and destroy what he calls terrorist infrastructure.

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:39.080
He describes the scale as unseen in the West Bank for decades, using a model from the Iron

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:39.900
Wall operation.

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:46.420
The UN Rights Office says that operation, from January 2025, forcibly displaced tens of thousands

00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:47.860
from northern refugee camps.

00:01:47.860 --> 00:01:52.200
troops. He blames Hamas for planning a major attack aimed at murdering innocent civilians.

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:57.200
Army Chief Ayal Zameer, says a large quantity of ammunition found in the gunman's vehicle,

00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:02.040
was meant for a larger attack. The army says dozens of later operations brought dozens

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:07.100
of arrests, including people affiliated with Hamas and Islamic Jihad, and the seizure of

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:12.600
M-16 rifles and submachine guns. Finance Minister Bezalel Smotrich calls for a West Bank

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:17.780
campaign exactly like in Gaza, including dismantling the Palestinian Authority. He says

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:20.140
that would be among the first demands of the next government.

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:24.980
National Security Minister Itamar Ben-Gvere says Palestinian freedom of movement should

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:29.500
be restricted because the lives of settlers, soldiers, and police are a million times

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:30.200
more important.

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:36.260
Former peace-now-director Yari V. Oppenheimer told Al Jazeera that demolitions, curfews, arrests,

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:41.000
and settler revenge attacks were likely, and that daily life for Palestinians was already

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:41.540
impossible.

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:45.360
Voters decide next Tuesday whether Netanyahu gets another term.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:48.940
firm, three years after the Hamas-led attacks that triggered the Gaza war.

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:53.889
Oleshki sits on the Russian-occupied bank of the Denebro, opposite Karsan.

00:02:54.429 --> 00:02:58.649
The White House said Friday that first lady Melania Trump helped broker a local ceasefire

00:02:58.649 --> 00:03:00.709
so aid can enter and civilians can leave.

00:03:01.189 --> 00:03:05.909
It says Ukraine and Russia agreed to pause military action, with the ceasefire set for October

00:03:05.909 --> 00:03:06.709
29th.

00:03:07.029 --> 00:03:11.529
She and a representative negotiated timing and procedures with both leaderships as what

00:03:11.529 --> 00:03:13.909
the White House calls an exclusive intermediary.

00:03:13.909 --> 00:03:18.949
Melania Trump says the town is a front-line war city on the brink of disaster, that those

00:03:18.949 --> 00:03:23.049
left are primarily elderly, and that they need medicine, food, and clean water.

00:03:23.409 --> 00:03:27.909
She says that without her intervention, aid and evacuation of the elderly would be impossible.

00:03:28.569 --> 00:03:34.569
United 24 media reports a White House estimate of 1700 to 2000 residents still there, mostly

00:03:34.569 --> 00:03:39.729
elderly, plus about 50 children, against about 24,000 before the full-scale invasion.

00:03:39.729 --> 00:03:45.429
No comprehensive census has been taken since 2022, about 90 percent of the city flooded

00:03:45.429 --> 00:03:48.209
when the Kakovka Dam collapsed in June 2023.

00:03:48.869 --> 00:03:53.789
Under the announced plan, civilian representatives from both sides would visit homes, and people

00:03:53.789 --> 00:03:57.949
who choose to leave would be taken either to Ukrainian control territory or to Russia.

00:03:58.509 --> 00:04:02.829
An American media organization would document the process, and the sides would coordinate

00:04:02.829 --> 00:04:05.549
demining of roads still contaminated with explosives.

00:04:05.549 --> 00:04:10.369
The White House did not say how long the pause would last, or how compliance would be watched.

00:04:10.789 --> 00:04:15.529
The Guardian says there is no comment yet from Moscow or from Ukraine, and that its correspondence

00:04:15.529 --> 00:04:17.529
are still trying to corroborate the statement.

00:04:18.149 --> 00:04:22.809
Ukrainian Human Rights Commissioner Demetro Lubinets said Friday that evacuation talks

00:04:22.809 --> 00:04:25.149
were still underway, though nearing completion.

00:04:25.689 --> 00:04:29.289
United 24 media says Ukraine has not officially confirmed the deal.

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:32.729
Each side has accused the other of blocking supplies since May,

00:04:32.729 --> 00:04:37.609
A stretch linked to deaths from starvation and disease, a destroyed morgue, and no running

00:04:37.609 --> 00:04:37.989
water.

00:04:38.429 --> 00:04:44.369
Pope Leo XIV urged Vladimir Putin on October 16th to accept a ceasefire so food and medicine

00:04:44.369 --> 00:04:45.369
could reach civilians.

00:04:45.829 --> 00:04:50.929
By October 19th, Kiev and Moscow were moving to finish an evacuation from Oleshky and

00:04:50.929 --> 00:04:56.429
six nearby settlements, where around 6,000 civilians, including up to 200 children, were

00:04:56.429 --> 00:04:57.189
believed to remain.

00:04:57.749 --> 00:05:02.369
The White House ties the channel to earlier contacts that it says, returned seven Ukrainian

00:05:02.369 --> 00:05:05.689
in children on April 2nd, and five more on July 30th.

00:05:06.601 --> 00:05:09.241
Jordan's government spokesman, Muhammad Al-Mamani,

00:05:09.481 --> 00:05:12.441
says gunmen killed six people and wounded 28 others

00:05:12.441 --> 00:05:15.081
Friday at a church funeral in the village of Hamud

00:05:15.081 --> 00:05:16.601
in the Karak governorate.

00:05:16.941 --> 00:05:18.721
A public security directorate account

00:05:18.721 --> 00:05:21.621
places the shooting at a Greek Orthodox church in Karak,

00:05:22.021 --> 00:05:24.321
about 180 kilometers south of Amman.

00:05:24.961 --> 00:05:27.001
Al-Jazeera reports at least seven killed,

00:05:27.181 --> 00:05:30.261
and says survivors describe two masked men opening fire

00:05:30.261 --> 00:05:32.341
as dozens attended the funeral procession.

00:05:32.901 --> 00:05:38.141
Warner Colled Burkhan told Al-Mamlaka Television that two attackers, with a rifle and a pistol,

00:05:38.641 --> 00:05:39.641
fired for several minutes.

00:05:40.261 --> 00:05:45.221
BBC verified CCTV appears to show three armed men moving from a road toward the church,

00:05:45.761 --> 00:05:49.281
two entering what looks like a vehicle entrance, then returning with a third.

00:05:49.881 --> 00:05:54.961
Al-Mamani calls the attack heinous, says security forces are deployed and investigating, and

00:05:54.961 --> 00:05:58.401
says the prime minister will chair a security council meeting of all ministers.

00:05:58.401 --> 00:06:02.881
others. No one has claimed responsibility. The gunmen were reported to have arrived by

00:06:02.881 --> 00:06:05.181
car and fled, and a manhunt is underway.

00:06:05.861 --> 00:06:10.321
Karak has a sizable Christian community in majority Muslim Jordan, and the BBC notes

00:06:10.321 --> 00:06:16.241
such violence is rare. In 2016, gunmen ambushed police in Karak, including at a crusader

00:06:16.241 --> 00:06:21.581
castle, killing 10 people, seven of them officers, before security forces killed the gunmen.

00:06:22.630 --> 00:06:28.010
Interior Minister Laurent Nunez says drive-by shootings Friday in traps, Southwest of Paris,

00:06:28.010 --> 00:06:34.050
and then in nearby La Vaire, killed one person and wounded five others, three seriously, in a

00:06:34.050 --> 00:06:40.310
rampage of almost 15 minutes. France 24 reports one killed and four wounded, including a 12-year-old

00:06:40.310 --> 00:06:45.070
girl, and says authorities suspect the attack may have been racially motivated. The New York

00:06:45.070 --> 00:06:50.330
Times says anti-terrorism prosecutors are exploring a racial or religious motive. The National

00:06:50.330 --> 00:06:55.230
Anti-terrorist Prosecutors Office says the case appears to be murder in connection with a terrorist

00:06:55.230 --> 00:07:00.830
underpriced, including acts tied to real or perceived race, ethnicity, nation, or religion.

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:04.810
Nunez told reporters and traps that it is clearly a terrorist crime.

00:07:05.430 --> 00:07:10.110
Mayor Ali Rabay says a man fired at random from a gray-renote Cleo at a petrol station,

00:07:10.550 --> 00:07:14.210
a medical center, and a playground, wanting as many casualties as possible.

00:07:14.630 --> 00:07:19.110
He says the person killed was of African origin, and one person in critical condition was

00:07:19.110 --> 00:07:23.630
of North African descent, and calls the attack racist and probably Islamophobic.

00:07:23.630 --> 00:07:27.450
The anti-terror prosecutor urges caution on the victim's identities.

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:34.170
A local police chief told BFM-TV the suspect used an older-style semi-automatic weapon in Bursts,

00:07:34.470 --> 00:07:37.530
and La Parisian reports the gun dated to the Second World War.

00:07:38.030 --> 00:07:44.630
The inquiry also covers possession of a Category A weapon and conspiracy with a terrorist group to prepare crimes against people.

00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:49.730
The suspected attacker, a 39-year-old known to police but not-to-intelligent services,

00:07:49.730 --> 00:07:51.870
local media report was arrested.

00:07:52.490 --> 00:07:55.870
Prime Minister Sebastian Lacornu's statement places that arrest in nearby

00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:56.650
coigners.

00:07:57.110 --> 00:07:58.950
Nunez says the mode of remains unclear.

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:03.400
President Emanuel Macron is set to meet student representatives Friday.

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:07.820
The first such meeting since the mobilization began ahead of Saturday's protests.

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:12.600
France 24 says those protests grew from high school complaints over school conditions.

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:16.640
Paris is extending a partial curfew in parts of the city until Monday.

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:21.060
Protests are banned in Marseille and Lyon, and only union demonstrations will

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:24.880
be authorized. 70,000 security personnel will deploy Saturday.

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:29.700
The Globe and Mail says those officers and John Dahms go out with helicopters, armored

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:34.500
vehicles, and water cannons, and that the Louvre and major Paris museums will close Saturday.

00:08:35.060 --> 00:08:39.660
The measures follow weekend looting in clashes that injured police officers and damaged stores.

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:45.360
Paris Saint-Germain's match was postponed after a police request, Al Jazeera reports, and

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:48.680
And Usman, Dembele, is to miss the ball-and-door event because of that move.

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:53.300
Aaron Rogers of the Pittsburgh Steelers says the NFL would cancel Sunday's game against

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:56.300
the New Orleans Saints in St. Denis if the city were unsafe.

00:08:56.840 --> 00:09:00.460
That ground is about 10 kilometers from where Saturday's protests are expected.

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:04.420
The student meeting is a scheduled talk, not an agreement yet announced.

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:10.140
Francis Tenure Bond yield has pushed above 5 percent for the first time since 2002, with

00:09:10.140 --> 00:09:13.020
